{"availability":"available","full":"Fraunhofer-AISEC/qml-playground","name":"qml-playground","description":"Quantum Machine Learning (QML) Playground is an interactive web application designed to visualize the inner workings of quantum machine learning models in an intuitive and educational manner.","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":41,"forks":12,"created":"2025-07-23T14:13:58Z","updated":"2026-07-17T22:44:41Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://websites.fraunhofer.de/qml-playground/","topics":["educational","machinelearning","paper","quantum","quantum-computing","quantum-machine-learning","visualization"],"demo":"https://websites.fraunhofer.de/qml-playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.864Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.864Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.864Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.864Z","stars":41,"forks":12}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Quantum Machine Learning (QML) Playground is an interactive web application designed to visualize and explore the inner workings of quantum machine learning models in an intuitive and educational way. Inspired by classical tools like TensorFlow Playground, it focuses on parameterized quantum circuits (PQCs) — particularly the data re-uploading universal quantum classifier — and introduces visual metaphors such as Bloch spheres and the Q-simplex to interpret quantum state evolution.","Now extended beyond classification, the playground also supports regression tasks, uncertainty quantification, and regularization techniques, enabling deeper exploration of quantum model performance and generalization.","This playground is ideal for learners, educators, and researchers who want to explore QML models without requiring deep expertise in quantum hardware or simulators."],"features":["🧠 Real-time QML model training and visualization","🌐 Visual Metaphors for Data and Quantum State Evolution"